            B.q("sa-m4-21", "sa-relational", "One tenant database cannot hold all tenants as the app grows to millions of users, and each request belongs to one tenant. How do you scale out the data in Azure SQL Database?", listOf("Shard tenants across databases, routed by an Elastic Database shard map", "Partition the tables by tenant ID inside the single database", "Send tenant requests to read scale-out replicas of the single database", "Move the single tenant database into an elastic pool"), setOf(0), "Sharding spreads tenants over many databases. A shard map, kept by the Elastic Database client library, records which database holds each tenant, so the app sends each request to the right one.",
